# R9 — No doc drift

If your change touches anything covered by these docs, update the relevant doc **in the same change set**:

| Code area | Doc(s) to update |
|---|---|
| `backend/src/services/MatchService.ts`, socket handlers, scoring, timer | [`docs/MATCH_FLOW.md`](mdc:docs/MATCH_FLOW.md) |
| `backend/src/config/gameConfig.ts`, `Assets/Scripts/Config/GameMatchConfig.cs` | [`docs/PLAN.md`](mdc:docs/PLAN.md), [`docs/AGENTS.md`](mdc:docs/AGENTS.md), the magic-values rule |
| `backend/src/rest/profile.ts`, `redeem.ts`, `economy.ts` | [`docs/PROFILE_AND_ECONOMY.md`](mdc:docs/PROFILE_AND_ECONOMY.md) |
| `backend/src/rest/social.ts`, `scoreboards.ts` | [`docs/SOCIAL_AND_SCOREBOARDS.md`](mdc:docs/SOCIAL_AND_SCOREBOARDS.md) |
| Any new Unity UIKit prefab / shell | [`docs/UI_CONTRACT.md`](mdc:docs/UI_CONTRACT.md), [`docs/SCREENS.md`](mdc:docs/SCREENS.md) |
| Any new privacy / consent change | [`docs/PRIVACY_AND_LEGAL.md`](mdc:docs/PRIVACY_AND_LEGAL.md) |
| New gameplay tunable | [`docs/AGENTS.md`](mdc:docs/AGENTS.md) (R5/R10) and the magic-values rule |

If you cannot find a clear home for the doc update, add a section to the most relevant file rather than skipping the update.
